this video is presented by tales of  arise  as fancy rpgs go very few have the  legacy of the tales of series with over  25 years and 16 main titles already  secured in both the hearts and gaming  collections of fans now with tales of a  rise not only are we going to be treated  to a new and masterfully crafted action  adventure rpg but a fully enhanced tales  of experience from the combat to the  characters and the entire world design  these exciting new changes and  improvements have so much to offer new  players and long time fans so whichever  camp you hail from let's take a look at  what you can expect from tales of arise  let's start with combat what's a quest  to challenge the fate of civilization  without a good kicking to the bad guys  the battle system has been enriched from  previous games in the series with combat  feeling fast and frenetic  fights take place in a closed 3d area  after an encounter giving you and the  team plenty of space to maneuver and  plan your attack  during the fight you'll control one of  the six main characters from your  adventure with three others making up  your team of four  each has their own strengths combat  style and perks that can wildly swing  the tide of battle so if you pride  yourself on the efficient slapping of  your enemies there's a lot of detail to  get into if you choose  your two protagonists alfin and shion  both have some awesome moves  alfin is a sword-wielding all-rounder  while xion sports a rifle that is great  against aerial enemies the rest of your  party is no different  lore is a hand-to-hand combat pro that  dominates rigid and armored enemies  rinwell is your magic user who also  pairs great against other magic users  kisara and her shield work well with  charging enemies and also protecting  allies while dohalin is ideal for  getting the nippy agile enemies with his  combat rod  the best part of the combat entails of  her eyes is seeing the team working  together in a seamless unit lighting up  the arena with dramatic combos and  special attacks that overwhelm your  enemies and leave you with a smug look  and a fistful of loot for your trouble  as with previous tales games there are  several ways to deal damage in a fight  your basic attack is free to use any  time and ideal to start getting early  hits on your combo counter  you can target weak points on certain  enemies to increase your chance of  breaking their guard and knocking them  down opening up a window for you and the  team to lay it on thick  next you have special techniques known  in the series as arts these are mapped  to three of your face buttons but  require charge from your arts gauge you  can see this just above your hp gauge  each art uses a particular amount of aeg  to perform so you can choose if you want  to save up for a bigger move or hammer  through cheaper attacks some arts will  even launch your enemies opening them up  to additional attacks in the air this  also changes your available arts from  ground to aerial giving you a total of  six to work with  as the game progresses you'll not only  unlock more arts and skills but also the  ability to use more than six in combat  of course getting damage in is all well  and good  great even  really great but unless you know how to  avoid it yourself these fights are going  to be short and painful with the  exception of kisara and her enormous  shield the other five characters can't  block attacks instead you'll be dodging  you can dodge in any direction you  choose but timing it just right will  give you a perfect dodge opening up a  window to counter attack your enemy  mastery of this is key to maintaining  the flow in battle and keeping the  pressure on so take some time early on  to get a feel for the movement future  you will thank you if you do take some  damage you can use healing and support  arts to recover your hp  beware though this uses up cure points  or cp that can usually only be recovered  from resting out of combat so avoiding  damage is always preferable  next you have your boost attacks you can  see each character charging their boost  gauge over their icon in the lower left  corner  as the team leader you can choose when  to trigger these by pressing the  corresponding button on the d-pad these  are powerful moves unique to each  character and have some handy special  effects  alfin for example can use some of his  own hp to do bonus damage while xi'an  can knock flying enemies out of the sky  but what if the boost attack you need  isn't in the active party  worry not you can still call in that  ally to jump in and perform the move  as you get more comfortable with the  battle system you'll master the timing  of boost attacks to give the maximum  impact for you and the team  where things get really dramatic are  with boost strikes  as you lay the damage on an enemy you'll  be building up its strike gauge  if it fills you'll get an on-screen  prompt to hit the d-pad and watch the  screen light up as two characters team  up to smash a boss or finish off lighter  foe  this is by far the most satisfying way  to end a fight and will contribute to  your battle score at the end the better  your score the more skill points you'll  get for upgrading your skills and titles  throughout the game  on rare occasions you'll also get the  strike prompt when certain conditions  are met so watch out for these  opportunities to see your teammates in  action doing their finest work  [Music]  now that you've got combat sorted let's  take a look at the stunning worlds  you'll be exploring on your adventure  welcome to the breathtaking landscapes  of dana and rena  tales of arise has a whole new look from  previous games in the series giving the  environment incredible scale and detail  using the atmospheric shader  the traditional anime look has been  modernized but longtime fans will still  recognize the style especially during  the skits and fully animated cut scenes  within the game  well this crew just gets bigger and  bigger tales of arise takes place across  multiple regions of two different worlds  the more medieval world of dana and the  advanced world of rena  renner has ruled over dana for 300 years  enslaving its people and soaking up  dana's resources for themselves now  divided up by walls and controlling  lords you and the party will have a huge  variety of regions to explore  from the dry desert regions of calaglia  dotted with oil refining machinery  to the snow-covered region of siselodia  each with unique characters to meet on  your quest  the region's a semi-open world meaning  you'll be moving through several smaller  open areas that aren't directly  connected to one another  fans of tales games will know all too  well that curiosity is often rewarded in  these areas so be sure to really take a  look around for resources and hidden  secrets  new to tales of arise is the ability to  jump over the terrain and swim in  shallow water opening up new options and  opportunities in the game  for newcomers you'll be glad to know  that you can keep your distance from  enemies you don't want to engage meaning  you'll always be ready for your next  fight  in the open world you'll want to make  sure you're managing your health and  cure points  out of combat it's usually best to heal  up using items such as gels rather than  burning through your cp as this precious  resource is also needed to unlock closed  paths to progress the game  and find hidden treasures  wow  you can rest up at campsites to recover  cp as well as engage in a bit of  delicious cooking  recipes will need different ingredients  of course but the bonus effects can help  you and the team both in and out of  combat so it's well worth dusting off  the old apron for good this came out  just the way i hoped you can even take  on farming of animals and crops as well  as fishing to help out with your  resource management  you'll also be coming across npcs out in  the wild and entire communities in the  towns  here you can trade items and resources  upgrade your gear and forge brand new  weapons to take into battle  each character has a main weapon armor  set and an accessory that you'll be  changing up as you go  your cosmetic style isn't directly tied  to your equipment though  costumes are a recurring feature in the  tails games freeing you up to craft your  own look with your favorite gear  speaking of which keep an eye out in the  world as you might spot an owl sitting  quietly by itself  go say hello and you'll be rewarded with  an interesting equippable item  as the characters in the game are now 3d  models rather than illustrations you'll  be able to see them in their costumes  during moments of dialogue  tails games have always put story and  character connections first and tales of  her eyes is no different  the relationship between the two  protagonists alfin and shion is  particularly difficult with alfin at  and shion are renin  [Music]  alfin has no memory of his past but is  driven by a desire to free his people  from the grasp of rena  as well as losing his memory he's also  lost the ability to feel pain  the somewhat handy trick that motivates  his hp sapping arts in combat  xi'an has allied herself with alfin  against her own people but is afflicted  with the curse of thorns hurting anyone  who touches her as a renin shion is also  able to draw and use astral energy a  power that resides in all living things  and use it in the form of astral arts  she's able to manifest this energy into  the blazing sword a weapon that burns  whoever wields it with alfin's ability  to withstand pain he becomes the only  person capable of grasping the sword but  also capable of any physical connection  with xion making their relationship all  the more complex  [Music]  as you explore the landscape you'll  quickly meet the rest of your allies and  begin forging the bonds that drive the  story of tales of arise for new players  you'll find a deep and engaging action  rpg with exciting combat and a rich  world to explore  for fans so much will feel familiar as  this much love series gets the enhanced  and modernized touches it deserves  tales of arise launches on september  10th ready for you to challenge the fate  of a world  [Music]  alfie  [Music]  [Applause]
 

